0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","3.12",{"topic":{"id":"3.12","title":"Cloud Forensics","minutes":15,"summary":"Investigate distributed services through tenant records, audit trails, snapshots, and provider cooperation rather than assuming access to a physical server.","sections":[{"title":"Service models and evidence control","body":["In infrastructure-as-a-service, a customer may control virtual disks, snapshots, operating-system logs, and network configuration while the provider controls the physical infrastructure. Platform and software services expose different logs and exports. Identify the service model, tenant, region, account, and subscription before planning acquisition.","A cloud “disk” is a distributed abstraction. Snapshot and export mechanisms may be more practical and less disruptive than attempting physical access. Record the snapshot identifier, source volume, consistency settings, creation time, encryption context, and export process. A snapshot can be crash-consistent rather than application-consistent, affecting interpretation."]},{"title":"Audit logs and identity events","body":["Control-plane logs record actions such as creating a snapshot, changing a policy, or issuing a token, while application logs record service-level events. They are not interchangeable. Examine actor identity, role, session, source context, requested action, result, and resource identifier. Service accounts and assumed roles can obscure the initiating human without additional correlation.","Cloud clocks, event delivery delays, and regional timestamps require careful normalization. Preserve the raw API response and query parameters, including pagination and filters. An export showing no events may reflect the wrong region, time range, or log source. Check retention, ingestion delay, and whether logging was enabled before the incident."]},{"title":"Provider cooperation and volatile services","body":["Containers, serverless functions, and autoscaled instances can disappear quickly. Preserve configuration, images, logs, and relevant runtime observations where authorized. A running container may contain useful state, but rebuilding from a known image does not recreate every runtime change. Document what the snapshot or capture actually includes.","Ask the provider for specific records through the competent route and explain preservation urgency. A customer cannot ordinarily seize a shared physical host. Cross-border storage and provider jurisdiction affect access. Present findings with the service boundary visible: “the tenant audit log records” is more precise than an unsupported statement about the provider’s entire infrastructure."]}],"practice":{"title":"Reconstruct a snapshot action","scenario":"A fictional cloud audit log shows a role creating and sharing a volume snapshot.","steps":["Identify the role, session, resource, action, region, and timestamp.","Correlate the role assumption with authentication records.","Preserve the complete paginated log response and query settings.","Separate the observed API action from the identity of the human operator."],"debrief":"Cloud attribution is a chain through identities, roles, sessions, and resources. One actor field is rarely the whole answer."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["bnss","bsa","dpdp"],"sources":["nist-guide","privacy","budapest","bsa"],"labId":"acquisition","unit":3,"objectives":["Explain service models and evidence control and apply it to an investigation.","Explain audit logs and identity events and apply it to an investigation.","Explain provider cooperation and volatile services and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-3.12","prompt":"Why is a cloud snapshot not always a complete forensic acquisition?","options":["It can never contain files.","Its consistency, scope, encryption, and service boundary may limit what it preserves.","Cloud providers do not use clocks.","It automatically includes every provider log."],"answer":1,"explanation":"A snapshot represents a defined resource and state; related logs, memory, and provider records may need separate preservation.","unit":3}}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
